{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeInclusion","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Bilinear","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.StrongRankCondition","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Constructions","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Finrank"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.finrank_le_factorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.finrank_le_factorial","kind":"theorem","line":423,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeCoset.lean#L423-L437","doc":"**The headline coset spanning bound** `dim_K H_{m+1}(q) ≤ (m+1)!`\n(`Hecke K q qi m = H_{m+1}(q)`), proved from `span_cosetFam_eq_top` and the\nfamily-cardinality count `card_cosetIndex`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.span_cosetFam_eq_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.span_cosetFam_eq_top","kind":"theorem","line":402,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeCoset.lean#L402-L421","doc":"**The coset family spans `H_{m+1}(q)`** (`span = ⊤`), from the right-handed\nclosure lemma `span_mul_gen_mem` via the adjoin-equals-span-of-submonoid route\n(exactly as `HeckeDim3.span_sixWords_eq_top` at `n = 3`, but inducting on the\nright). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.span_mul_gen_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.span_mul_gen_mem","kind":"theorem","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeCoset.lean#L329-L400","doc":"**The coset-span closure lemma (the crux) — right-handed.**  *Right*\nmultiplication by any generator `σ_i` of `H_{m+1}(q) = Hecke K q qi m` preserves\nthe `K`-span of the coset family `cosetFam m`.\n\nThis is the general-`n` form of the twelve explicit `HeckeDim3.gen_mul_mem`\nreductions at `n = 3`, and it is **sorry-free**: each family element\n`ι(w)·r_j` meets `σ_i` in exactly one of the four cases of the bubble\n(`descProd_mul_σ_of_add_lt` / `_of_add_eq` / `_of_add_eq_succ` / `_of_le_add`,\nselected by comparing `i + j` with `m`), and every case returns either a family\nelement or `ι(w·σ_k)·r_j` with the level-`m` statement available by recursion.\n\n**Why right and not left.**  The family is `ι(H_m)·r_j`, with the subalgebra on\nthe *left*.  Right multiplication therefore acts on the `r_j` factor, where the\nHecke relations apply; left multiplication by the top generator would have to\nmove `σ_m` past the opaque `ι(w)`, which no relation does.  Taking the induction\non the correct side is what turns this from \"the deep half of the basis theorem\"\ninto a four-case computation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.incl_mul_descProd_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.incl_mul_descProd_mem","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeCoset.lean#L307-L327","doc":"**Coset absorption.**  For any `w` in the span of the level-`m` family and any\ncoset index `k`, the product `ι(w)·r_k` lies in the span of the level-`(m+1)`\nfamily (it *is* a family element when `w` is one). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.one_mem_span_cosetFam","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.one_mem_span_cosetFam","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeCoset.lean#L281-L303","doc":"`1` lies in the span of the coset family (sorry-free, by induction on `m`).\nBase: `cosetFam 0 () = 1`.  Step: `1 = ι(1)·r_0 = ι(cosetFam m b₁)·descProd m 0`\nwhere `b₁` witnesses `1 ∈ span (range (cosetFam m))`; since `heckeIncl` is an\nalgebra map and `descProd m 0 = 1`, the image of `1` is `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.finrank_le_card_of_span","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.finrank_le_card_of_span","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeCoset.lean#L273-L279","doc":"Generic reduction: a finite set spanning `⊤` bounds the finrank by its card. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.cosetFam_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.cosetFam_succ","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeCoset.lean#L267-L269","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.cosetFam","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.cosetFam","kind":"def","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeCoset.lean#L260-L265","doc":"The coset spanning family `cosetFam m : cosetIndex m → Hecke K q qi m`.\n`cosetFam 0 () = 1`; `cosetFam (m+1) (b, j) = ι(cosetFam m b) · r_j`, where\n`ι = heckeIncl` is the tower inclusion and `r_j = descProd m j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.card_cosetIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.card_cosetIndex","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeCoset.lean#L251-L258","doc":"`Fintype.card (cosetIndex m) = (m+1)!` — the family has `(m+1)!` elements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.instFintypeCosetIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.instFintypeCosetIndex","kind":"instance","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeCoset.lean#L245-L249","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.cosetIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.cosetIndex","kind":"def","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeCoset.lean#L237-L243","doc":"The finite index type of the coset spanning family of `Hecke K q qi m`.\n`cosetIndex 0 = Unit`; `cosetIndex (m+1) = cosetIndex m × Fin (m+2)` — one factor\n`Fin (m+2)` for the `m+2` coset representatives added at each tower step.\n`Fintype.card (cosetIndex m) = (m+1)!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.descProd_mul_σ_of_le_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.descProd_mul_σ_of_le_add","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeCoset.lean#L169-L233","doc":"**Braid** (`m + 2 ≤ i + j`): `σ_i` lies strictly inside `r_j`, and the\nYang–Baxter move plus far commutation pull `σ_{i-1}` out on the left. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.descProd_mul_σ_of_add_eq_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.descProd_mul_σ_of_add_eq_succ","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeCoset.lean#L153-L167","doc":"**Quadratic** (`i + j = m + 1`, `j ≥ 1`): `σ_i` is the *last* factor of `r_j`,\nso `r_j σ_i = r_{j-1} σ_i²`, and the Hecke quadratic relation splits it into\n`r_j` and `r_{j-1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.descProd_mul_σ_of_add_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.descProd_mul_σ_of_add_eq","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeCoset.lean#L145-L151","doc":"**Lengthening** (`i + j = m`): appending `σ_i` to `r_j` is exactly the\nrecursive step defining `r_{j+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.descProd_mul_σ_of_add_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.descProd_mul_σ_of_add_lt","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeCoset.lean#L131-L143","doc":"**Far commutation** (`i + j + 1 ≤ m`): `σ_i` sits at least two below every\nfactor of `r_j`, so it commutes past the whole descending product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.descProd_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.descProd_succ","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeCoset.lean#L102-L104","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.descProd_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.descProd_zero","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeCoset.lean#L100-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.descProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.descProd","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeCoset.lean#L91-L98","doc":"The descending product `descProd m j = σ_m σ_{m-1} ⋯ σ_{m-j+1}` of the top\n`j` generators of `H_{m+1}(q) = Hecke K q qi (m+1)` (length `j`; `descProd m 0 = 1`).\nThis is the coset representative `r_j` in the decomposition\n`H_{m+1} = Σ_j ι(H_m)·r_j`.  The generator index `m - j` (truncated subtraction)\nis always `< m + 1`, so no bound hypothesis is needed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}